.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Env
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.test

# Wrangler's local secrets for `pnpm sync:dev` — this is where a real pairing
# phrase would sit, and it is not covered by the .env rules above.
.dev.vars
.dev.vars.*

# Vite
vite.config.js.timestamp-*
vite.config.ts.timestamp-*

# direnv
.direnv/

# Nix
result
result-*

# Claude Code worktrees — not used here (see CLAUDE.md), but old ones linger
.claude/worktrees/

# Rust
/target

# The core compiled to wasm plus its wasm-bindgen glue — `pnpm core:wasm`
# writes it, every `pnpm dev|build|test|check` runs that first.
/src/lib/db/wasm/

# Tauri's generated ACL schemas, written by `tauri-build` on every desktop build.
# Its sibling `gen/android` *is* committed — it carries an icon set and an
# edge-to-edge fix that only exist as edits to the generated project, and it
# cannot be regenerated on a machine with no Android SDK (docs/desktop.md).
# What `tauri android build` rewrites per run is ignored by the generated
# project's own nested `.gitignore` files.
/crates/sapling-desktop/gen/schemas/

# `tauri icon` writes a desktop and iOS set beside the Android mipmaps it is
# run for, and there is no flag to ask for one platform. Nothing reads these —
# `bundle.icon` points straight at `static/icons/icon-512.png` and bundling is
# off — so they are a side effect, not an artifact.
/crates/sapling-desktop/icons/
